      "writtenOn": "2021-01-26T09:21:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CLAT is Android specific feature.\n\nIn the initial version, clatd daemon read and translate packets.\nCurrently, it uses eBPF but there is no clue that bpf_skb_proto_6_to_4 should support UDP GRO fraglist.\nIt is a new feature and needs many line changes.\n\nFor upstream, Steffen Klassert (UDP GRO fraglist writer) said\nin https://lore.kernel.org/patchwork/patch/1362257/\n\"The initial idea when I implemented this was to have a fast\nforwarding path for UDP. So forwarding is a usecase, but NAT\nis a problem, indeed.\"\n\nWe might cannot disable UDP GRO forwarding in upstream.\nSo I suggested Android specific workaround until UDP GRO get stable.",
      "parentUuid": "099f237f_fec97bfb",
      "revId": "082367f6969f9d9e220c5ab326f8ecad10ad2c9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
